"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nAn important early work that determined the direction of Detective Kyoichiro Kaga, who occupies a significant weight in the author's worldview.  \nIt is said to be a monumental work where he first appears as a professional detective belonging to the Metropolitan Police Department.  \n\nDetective Kaga focuses on why, the motive for the crime, rather than , the method of the crime.  \nAn investigation method based on empathy and psychological insight is said to be his symbolic feature that also appears in subsequent series.  \n\nShould I call it a ?  \nThis work can be said to be a somewhat complex work where romance, mystery, and human desire are intricately mixed.  \n\nA unique situation is created where the detective's personal emotional involvement becomes a weakness in solving the case and simultaneously an essential tool for uncovering the truth.  \n\nThe world of  is depicted as a microcosm of a competitive closed society where extreme psychological pressure, eating disorders, and cruel competition are hidden under the names of physical perfection and artistic expression.  \nThis closely links the background of the case with the theme.  "